{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"surface","tool":"read_skill","arguments":{"name":"json-xs-compact"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Compact JSON using json_xs\n\nUse to squash formatted JSON into one compact line without extra spaces.\n\nCall run_program with args [\"-f\", \"json\", \"-t\", \"json\"] and the actual JSON text as stdin (decode any transport string escaping first).\n\nVerified input: an outer array containing [1, 2], [3, \"x\"], and true with indentation and a trailing newline. Program exited 0 with empty stderr and stdout [[1,2],[3,\"x\"],true], without a trailing newline. Check stdout parses as JSON, preserves nesting, order, types and values, and has no formatting whitespace outside strings. Return program stdout exactly when asked."}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
