{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"surface","tool":"save_skill","arguments":{"name":"json-xs-perl-dumper","content":"# Convert JSON to a Perl data structure\n\nUse when asked to display JSON as Perl in Data::Dumper style. Run run_program with args [\"-f\", \"json\", \"-t\", \"dumper\"] and exact decoded JSON text on stdin.\n\nVerified with stdin `[1, \"two\", null]\\n`: exit 0, empty stderr, stdout is a bracketed Perl array with two-space indentation, numeric 1, double-quoted \"two\", and undef for JSON null, followed by a newline. The dumper format emits a bare structure without a $VAR1 assignment. Check array order, values and Perl null mapping, and return stdout exactly. --help is unsupported and exits 255 with usage."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
